{"questions":[{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860781a","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860781a","q":"<p>If the corner points of the feasible solution are (0, 10), (2, 2) and (4, 0), then the point of minimum z = 3x + 2y is ______.</p>","options":["<p>(2, 2)</p>","<p>(2, 2)</p>","<p>(0, 10)</p>","<p>(0, 10)</p>","<p>(4, 0)</p>","<p>(4, 0)</p>","<p>(3, 4)</p>","<p>(2, 4)</p>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>If the corner points of the feasible solution are (0, 10), (2, 2) and (4, 0), then the point of minimum z = 3x + 2y is <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>(2, 2)</strong></span>.</p>\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n<p>Z = 3x + 2y</p>\n<p>At (0, 10) = Z = 0 + 2 (10) = 20</p>\n<p>At (2, 2), = Z = 3 (2) + 2 (2) = 10</p>\n<p>At (4, 0), Z = 3 (4) + 0 = 12</p>\n<p>The minimum value of Z is 10 and it occurs at (2, 2).</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Linear Programming Problems","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"multipleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607828","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607828","q":"<p><strong>Find the feasible solution of the following inequation:</strong></p>\n<p>2x + 3y ≤ 6, x + y ≥ 2, x ≥ 0, y ≥<strong> </strong>0</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>First we draw the lines AB and CB whose equations are 2x + 3y = 6 and  x + y = 2 respectively.</p>\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"width: 99.4334%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%;\"><strong>Line</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%;\"><strong>Equation</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%;\"><strong>Points on the X-axis</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%;\"><strong>Points on the Y-axis</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%;\"><strong>Sign</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.9338%;\"><strong>Region</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%;\">AB</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%;\">2x + 3y = 6</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%;\">A (3,0)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%;\">B (0,2)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%; text-align: center;\">≤</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.9338%;\">origin side of line AB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%;\">CB</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%;\">x + y = 2</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%;\">C (2,0)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%;\">B(0,2)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.6748%; text-align: center;\">≥</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.9338%;\">non-origin side of line CB</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><img height=\"281\" src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fhsc_maharashtra%252F12%252Fpublic%252F6941afe8e3720f1c028af4fe.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afe8e3720f1c028af4fe.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afe8e3720f1c028af4fe.png?alt=media\" width=\"465\"/></p>\n<p>The feasible solution is ΔABC which is shaded in the graph.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Linear Programming Problems","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607896","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607896","q":"<p><strong>Solve the Linear Programming problem graphically:</strong></p>\n<p>Maximize z = 3x + 5y subject to x + 4y ≤ 24, 3x + y ≤ 21, x + y ≤ 9, x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0 also find the maximum value of z.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>To draw the feasible region, construct table as follows:</p>\n<table border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Inequality</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">x + 4y ≤ 24</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">3x + y ≤ 21</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">x + y ≤ 9</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Corresponding equation (of line)</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">x + 4y = 24</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">3x + y = 21</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">x + y = 9</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Intersection of line with X-axis</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(24, 0)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(7, 0)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(9, 0)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Intersection of line with Y-axis</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(0, 6)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(0, 21)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(0, 9)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Region</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Origin side</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Origin side</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Origin side</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0 represent 1<sup>st</sup> quadrant.</p>\n<p>Shaded portion OABCD is the feasible region, whose vertices are O(0, 0), A(7, 0), B, C and D(0, 6).</p>\n<p>B is the point of intersection of the lines 3x + y = 21 and x + y = 9.</p>\n<p>Solving the above equations, we get</p>\n<p>x = 6, y = 3</p>\n<p>∴ B ≡ (6, 3)</p>\n<p>C is the point of intersection of the lines x + 4y = 24 and x + y = 9.</p>\n<p>Solving the above equations, we get</p>\n<p>x = 4, y = 5</p>\n<p>∴ C ≡ (4, 5)</p>\n<p>Here, the objective function is Z = 3x + 5y</p>\n<p>∴ Z at O(0, 0) = 3(0) + 5(0) = 0</p>\n<p>Z at A(7, 0) = 3(7) + 5(0) = 21</p>\n<p>Z at B(6, 3) = 3(6) + 5(3) = 18 + 15 = 33</p>\n<p>Z at C(4, 5) = 3(4) + 5(5) = 12 + 25 = 37</p>\n<p>Z at D(0, 6) = 3(0) + 5(6) = 30</p>\n<p>∴ Z has maximum value 37 at C(4, 5).</p>\n<p>∴ Z has maximum value 37 when x = 4, y = 5.<br/><img height=\"377\" src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fhsc_maharashtra%252F12%252Fpublic%252F6941b002e3720f1c028af50b.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941b002e3720f1c028af50b.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941b002e3720f1c028af50b.png?alt=media\" width=\"401\"/></p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Linear Programming Problems","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperDate":"2025-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860786a","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860786a","q":"<p><strong>Solve the following L.P.P. by graphical method:</strong></p>\n<p>Maximize: Z = 10x + 25y <br/>subject to 0 ≤ x ≤ 3, <br/>0 ≤ y ≤ 3, <br/>x + y ≤ 5.<br/>Also find the maximum value of z.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p><strong>To draw the feasible region, construct table as follows:</strong></p>\n<table border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>Inequality</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">x ≤ 3</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">y ≤ 3</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">x + y ≤ 5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>Corresponding equation (of line)</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">x = 3</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">y = 3</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">x + y = 5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>Intersection of line with X-axis</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">(3, 0)</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">–</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">(5, 0)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>Intersection of line with Y-axis</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">–</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">(0, 3)</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">(0, 5)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>Region</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">Origin side</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">Origin side</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">Origin side</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Shaded portion OABCD is the feasible region, </p>\n<p>whose vertices are O(0, 0), A(3, 0), B, C and D(0, 3)</p>\n<p>B is the point of intersection of the lines x = 3 and x + y = 5.</p>\n<p>Substituting x = 3 in x + y = 5, we get y = 2</p>\n<p>∴ B ≡ (3, 2)</p>\n<p>C is the point of intersection of the lines y = 3 and x + y = 5.</p>\n<p>Substituting y = 3 in x + y = 5, we get</p>\n<p>x = 2</p>\n<p>∴ C ≡ (2, 3)<br/><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fhsc_maharashtra%252F12%252Fpublic%252F6941affae3720f1c028af508.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941affae3720f1c028af508.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941affae3720f1c028af508.png?alt=media\"/><br/>Here, the objective function is Z = 10x + 25y</p>\n<p>∴ Z at O(0, 0) = 10(0) + 25(0) = 0</p>\n<p>Z at A(3, 0) = 10(3) + 25(0) = 30</p>\n<p>Z at B(3, 2) = 10(3) + 25(2) = 30 + 50 = 80</p>\n<p>Z at C(2, 3) = 10(2) + 25(3) = 20 + 75 = 95</p>\n<p>Z at D(0, 3) = 10(0) + 25(3) = 75</p>\n<p>∴ Z has a maximum value of 95 at C(2, 3).</p>\n<p>∴ Z is maximum when x = 2 and y = 3.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Linear Programming Problems","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d148607812","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d148607812","q":"<p><strong>Solve the following LPP by graphical method:</strong></p>\n<p>Minimize z = 8x + 10y, subject to 2x + y ≥ 7, 2x + 3y ≥ 15, y ≥ 2, x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>First we draw the lines AB, CD and EF whose equations are 2x + y = 7, 2x + 3y = 15 and y = 2 respectively.</p>\n<table border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>Line</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>Equation</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>Points on the X-axis</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>Points on the Y-axis</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>Sign</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>Region</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">AB</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2x + y = 7</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">A(3.5, 0)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">B(0, 7)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">≥</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">non-origin side of line AB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">CD</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2x + 3y = 15</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">C(7.5, 0)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">D(0, 5)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">≥</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">non-origin side of line CD</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">EF</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">y = 2</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">–</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F(0, 2)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">≥</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">non-origin side of line EF</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><img height=\"377\" src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fhsc_maharashtra%252F12%252Fpublic%252F6941afe4e3720f1c028af4fc.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afe4e3720f1c028af4fc.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afe4e3720f1c028af4fc.png?alt=media\" width=\"349\"/><br/>The feasible region is EPQBY which is shaded in the graph. The vertices of the feasible region are P, Q and B(0, 7). P is the point of intersection of the lines 2x + 3y = 15 and y = 2.</p>\n<p>Substituting y = 2 in 2x + 3y = 15, we get</p>\n<p>2x + 3(2) = 15</p>\n<p>∴ 2x = 9</p>\n<p>∴ x = 4.5 </p>\n<p>∴ P = (4.5, 2)</p>\n<p>Q is the point of intersection of the lines</p>\n<p>2x + 3y = 15         .....(1)</p>\n<p>and 2x + y = 7      .....(2)</p>\n<p>On subtracting, we get</p>\n<p>2y = 8</p>\n<p>∴ y = 4</p>\n<p>∴ from (2), 2x + 4 = 7</p>\n<p>∴ 2x = 3</p>\n<p>∴ x = 1.5</p>\n<p>∴ Q = (1.5, 4)</p>\n<p>The values of the objective function z = 8x + 10y at these vertices are</p>\n<p>z(P) = 8(4.5) + 10(2) = 36 + 20 = 56</p>\n<p>z(Q) = 8(1.5) + 10(4) = 12 + 40 = 52</p>\n<p>z(B) = 8(0) + 10(7) = 70</p>\n<p>∴ z has minimum value 52, when x = 1.5 and y = 4</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Linear Programming Problems","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077e3","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077e3","q":"<p> Maximize: z = 3x + 5y  Subject to</p>\n<p>x +4y ≤ 24                3x + y  ≤ 21 </p>\n<p>x + y ≤ 9                     x ≥ 0 , y ≥0</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<table border=\"1\" style=\"width: 100%; height: 127px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 52px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 52px;\">Inequation</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 52px;\">Point on x-axis </td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 52px;\">Point on y-axis</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 52px;\">Feasible Region </td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px;\">x +4y ≤ 24</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px;\"> (24,0)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px;\">(0,6)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px;\">Origin side</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px;\">3x +y ≤ 21</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px;\">(7,0)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px;\">(0,21)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px;\">Origin side</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px;\">x + y ≤9</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px;\">(9,0)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px;\">(0,9)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px;\">Origin side</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fhsc_maharashtra%252F12%252Fpublic%252F6941afdce3720f1c028af4f9.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afdce3720f1c028af4f9.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afdce3720f1c028af4f9.png?alt=media\"/></p>\n<p>From the figure common feasible region is ABCDEA <br/>E is the point of intersection of  x + y = 9 and x + 4y =24<br/>Solving them we get E(4,5)<br/>D is the point of intersection of  x + y = 9 and 3x +y = 21<br/>Solving them we get D(6,3)</p>\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"width: 100%; height: 150px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center; height: 25px;\">End Point</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center; height: 25px;\">Value of z = 3x +5y</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 25px;\">A(0,6)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 25px;\">0 +30= 30 </td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 25px;\">B(0,0)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 25px;\">0 + 0 = 0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 25px;\">C(7,0)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 25px;\">21 + 0 = 21</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 25px;\">D(6,3)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 25px;\">18 +1 5 = 33</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 25px;\">E(4,5)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; height: 25px;\">12 +25 = <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">37</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>∴ z is maximum 37 at the point (4, 5) </p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Linear Programming Problems","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperDate":"2019-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077b2","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077b2","q":"<p><strong>Solve the following LPP by graphical method:</strong></p>\n<p>Minimize Z = 7x + y subject to 5x + y ≥ 5, x + y ≥ 3, x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>First we draw the lines AB and CD whose equations are 5x + y = 5  and  x + y = 3 respectively.</p>\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"width: 97.0282%; height: 46px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">Line</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">Inequation</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">Points on x</td>\n<td style=\"width: 10%; height: 18px;\">Points on y</td>\n<td style=\"width: 10%;\">Sign</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">Feasible region</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">AB</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">5x + y = 5</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">A(1,0)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 10%; height: 18px;\">B(0,5)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 10%; text-align: center;\">≥</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">Non - origin side AB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 20%;\">CD</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%;\">x + y = 3</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%;\">C(3,0)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 10%;\">D(0,3)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 10%; text-align: center;\">≥</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%;\">Non - origin side of line CD</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>1 unit = 1 cm both axis</p>\n<p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fhsc_maharashtra%252F12%252Fpublic%252F6941afd4e3720f1c028af4f3.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afd4e3720f1c028af4f3.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afd4e3720f1c028af4f3.png?alt=media\"/></p>\n<p>common feasible region BPC</p>\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"width: 70.409%; height: 82px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 27.0197%; height: 18px;\">Points</td>\n<td style=\"width: 72.9803%; height: 18px;\">Minimize z =  7x + y</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 27.0197%; height: 18px;\">B(0,5)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 72.9803%; height: 18px;\">Z(B) = 7(0) + 5 = 5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 27.0197%; height: 18px;\">`P(1/2, 5/2)`</td>\n<td style=\"width: 72.9803%; height: 18px;\">`Z(P) = 7xx1/2+5/2 = 6`</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 27.0197%; height: 18px;\">C(3,0)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 72.9803%; height: 18px;\">Z(C) = 7x(3) + 0 = 21</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Z is minimum at x = 0, y = 5 and min (z) = 5</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Linear Programming Problems","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperDate":"2018-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d14860778a","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d14860778a","q":"<p>Solve the following LPP by using graphical method.</p>\n<p>Maximize : Z = 6x + 4y</p>\n<p>Subject to x ≤ 2, x + y ≤  3, -2x + y ≤  1, x ≥  0, y ≥ 0.</p>\n<p>Also find maximum value of Z.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<table style=\"height: 142px;\" width=\"401\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\">Inequalities</td>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\">x ≤ 2</td>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\">x+y≤3</td>\n<td style=\"width: 94px;\">-2x+y≤1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\">Equalities</td>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\">x=2</td>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\">x+y=3</td>\n<td style=\"width: 94px;\">-2x+y=1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\">Intercept form</td>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\">\n<p>`x/2=1`</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\">\n<p>`x/3+y/3=1`</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 94px;\">\n<p>`x/(-1/2)+y/1=1`</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\">Origin Test</td>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\">0≤2</td>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\">0+0≤3</td>\n<td style=\"width: 94px;\">-2(0)+0≤1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\"> </td>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\">True Origin Side</td>\n<td style=\"width: 93px;\">True Origin Side</td>\n<td style=\"width: 94px;\">True Origin Side</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fhsc_maharashtra%252F12%252Fpublic%252F6941afcfe3720f1c028af4ef.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afcfe3720f1c028af4ef.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afcfe3720f1c028af4ef.png?alt=media\"/></p>\n<p>Shaded portion OABC is the feasible region, Where O(0,0) A(2, 0) D(0, 1), B(2, 1)</p>\n<p>For C :</p>\n<p>   x + y = 3 <br/><br/>– 2x + y = 1<br/><br/>   –   –      –<br/><br/>----------------------<br/><br/>   3x = 2</p>\n<p>∴ x = 2/3</p>\n<p>2/3+y=3 i.e y=7/3</p>\n<p>`∴ c(2/3,7/3)`</p>\n<p>Z = 6x + 4y</p>\n<p>Z at O(0, 0) = 6(0) + 4(0) = 0</p>\n<p>Z at A(2, 0) = 6(2) + 4(0) = 12</p>\n<p>Z at B(2, 1) = 6(2) + 4(1) = 16</p>\n<p>Z at `c(2/3,7/3)=6(2/3)+(7/3)4=40/3`</p>\n<p>Z at D(0,1) = 6(0) + 4(1) = 4 Thus, Z is maximized at B(2, 1) and its maximum value is 16.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Linear Programming Problems","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperDate":"2017-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"}]}